      "title": "Collaborative Requirements Development Methodology",
      "pageStart": 6,
      "pageEnd": 6,
      "target": "../sections/sec-007-collaborative-requirements-development-methodolo.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The collaborative requirements development methodology (CRDM) was developed initially by the Public \nHealth Informatics Institute in conjunction with PATH in 2009. The first broad application of this \nmethodology was in the domain of logistic management and supply chain, completed in 2010. While the \nmethodology was successful and appropriate for the supply chain, it was not clear if it could be applied \nequally effectively to the clinical domains and make sense to clinical stakeholders. Several smaller \nprojects (tuberculosis [TB] process flows in Tanzania and work on primary health service d",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
