      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Application of the Process to Clinical Work",
      "pageStart": 6,
      "pageEnd": 7,
      "target": "../sections/sec-008-application-of-the-process-to-clinical-work.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "One of the most significant initial barriers to using CRDM and business process mapping for clinical care \nwas language. Clinicians in particular often do not think of their activities as “business” activities. Careful \nexplanations and flexibility in using such terms allowed participants to quickly become more involved in \nthe process, as they could see how these business processes were accurately reflecting their work. \nAnother challenge was in recording activities and decisions consistently at the same level for each process \nmap. Depending on the expertise and specialization of the partici",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
