      "pageStart": 10,
      "pageEnd": 11,
      "target": "../sections/sec-012-conclusions.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "While the CRDM process has proven to yield very effective tools for creating a common language to \ndescribe the “work” of maternal care, this project has uncovered several opportunities to take the process \neven further. First, there is an immediate opportunity to generalize the language and processes to allow \nthem to be applied to other clinical areas and services. This is critical not only to promote reuse, but also \nto help recognize and design for single solutions that may be applied to improve all health services. This \nis critical in addressing the issue of siloed care that so often pla",
